            <ArticleTitle>Osteochondral autograft transplantation for osteochondritis dissecans of the scaphoid: case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>820-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jhsa.2011.02.019</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This report presents the case of a 36-year-old man who was arthroscopically diagnosed with symptomatic osteochondritis dissecans of the scaphoid. We treated the condition using osteochondral autograft transplantation.</AbstractText>
